{:edb/db-before-t 5366 :edb/db-after-t 5367 :edb/tx-data [[13194139538679 50 #inst "2026-10-21T16:20:56.925Z" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186068840 1038 #edb/ref 17592186671842 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186068840 1038 #edb/ref 17592186671846 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186068840 1038 #edb/ref 17592186671850 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186068840 1038 #edb/ref 17592186671852 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186068840 1038 #edb/ref 17592186671866 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186068840 1040 #edb/ref 17592186551645 13194139538679 17592186045443 false] [17592186068840 1040 #edb/ref 17592186671874 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671839 1080 "y=\\sqrt[3]{C + 2 x^{2}}" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671839 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671839 1083 #uuid "0290a6d7-2380-5108-8789-71bfb77109ab" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671840 1080 "y=\\ln{\\left(C + \\left(x - 8\\right)^{2} \\right)}" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671840 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671840 1083 #uuid "031a129f-52d6-5681-914e-7769e63f4f73" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671841 1080 "y=\\left(C + 3 \\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}\\right)^{3}" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671841 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671841 1083 #uuid "08259c26-cd01-57fc-8bd4-97710fe61f79" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671842 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671871 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671842 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671842 1071 "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y′=\\left(6 x + 42\\right)\\sqrt[3]{y^2}.$ Work on intervals where $y\\ne 0$; cube roots are real." 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671842 1072 #uuid "1b625cbe-e98e-52a2-876f-b8846d653bd3" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671842 1074 "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y′ & =\\left(6 x + 42\\right)\\sqrt[3]{y^2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{y^2}}\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =2 x + 14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{y^2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\int 2 x + 14\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{y} & =\\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution in implicit form is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{y}=\\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ Solving for $y$ gives\n\n$$\ny=\\left(C + \\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}\\right)^{3}.\n$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant." 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671843 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671848 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671843 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671857 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671843 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671858 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671843 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671870 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671843 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671873 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671843 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671843 1077 "selection" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671843 1078 #edb/ref 17592186671870 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671843 1079 #uuid "1cb0fb69-bacc-5d3c-a375-f02460cca2ea" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671844 1080 "y=\\sqrt[3]{C + 2 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671844 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671844 1083 #uuid "1efe4088-e51b-5797-a073-9e5ef1be0ff5" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671845 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671840 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671845 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671855 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671845 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671856 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671845 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671863 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671845 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671867 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671845 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671845 1077 "selection" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671845 1078 #edb/ref 17592186671855 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671845 1079 #uuid "263632f2-df73-5f67-9e44-f172ab629be2" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671846 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671853 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671846 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671846 1071 "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y′=\\frac{6 x - 12}{3 y^{2}}.$ Work on intervals where $y\\ne 0$; cube roots are real." 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671846 1072 #uuid "349ca8c0-aa18-5536-91e2-5228615e320b" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671846 1074 "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y′ & =\\frac{6 x - 12}{3 y^{2}} \\\\ 3 y^{2}\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =6 x - 12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3 y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\int 6 x - 12\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ y^{3} & =3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution in implicit form is\n\n$$\ny^{3}=3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ Solving for $y$ gives\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt[3]{C + 3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant." 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671847 1080 "y=\\left(C + \\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}\\right)^{3}" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671847 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671847 1083 #uuid "389dcd83-3be6-5ae7-8536-11e51af3d592" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671848 1080 "y=\\sqrt[3]{C + 3 \\left(x + 4\\right)^{2}}" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671848 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671848 1083 #uuid "40de40ea-de47-5945-83e5-48552756376d" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671849 1080 "y=\\left(C - \\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}\\right)^{3}" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671849 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671849 1083 #uuid "4cc19ee9-085a-53a3-9ebd-784a3aa3752f" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671850 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671845 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671850 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671850 1071 "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y′=\\left(x - 8\\right) e^{- y}.$ Work on intervals where the logarithm argument is positive." 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671850 1072 #uuid "4e2e674b-0850-5368-88f6-14e03d6bfda5" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671850 1074 "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y′ & =\\left(x - 8\\right) e^{- y} \\\\ e^{y}\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =x - 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int e^{y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\int x - 8\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ e^{y} & =\\frac{\\left(x - 8\\right)^{2}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution in implicit form is\n\n$$\ne^{y}=\\frac{\\left(x - 8\\right)^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ Solving for $y$ gives\n\n$$\ny=\\ln{\\left(C + \\frac{\\left(x - 8\\right)^{2}}{2} \\right)}.\n$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant." 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671851 1080 "y=\\sqrt[3]{C - x^{2}}" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671851 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671851 1083 #uuid "4ed6957e-4f4f-56e4-b4ca-d10746070f85" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671852 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671843 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671852 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671852 1071 "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y′=\\frac{- 4 x - 16}{3 y^{2}}.$ Work on intervals where $y\\ne 0$; cube roots are real." 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671852 1072 #uuid "56a509c2-c05b-5e8a-a692-10fa903b3237" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671852 1074 "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y′ & =\\frac{- 4 x - 16}{3 y^{2}} \\\\ 3 y^{2}\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =- 4 x - 16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3 y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\int - 4 x - 16\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ y^{3} & =- 2 \\left(x + 4\\right)^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution in implicit form is\n\n$$\ny^{3}=- 2 \\left(x + 4\\right)^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ Solving for $y$ gives\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt[3]{C - 2 \\left(x + 4\\right)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant." 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671853 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671844 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671853 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671859 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671853 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671860 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671853 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671865 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671853 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671872 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671853 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671853 1077 "selection" 13194139538679 17592186045443 true] [17592186671853 10